# Top-level bare heading

This top-level section is authored as a bare markdown `#` heading. It must
lift to a canonical `<section>` element with a proper `<section-title>`, not
flow through as `<h1>`.

## Bare sub-heading with *emphasis* in the title

The bare `##` heading lifts to `<sub-section>`. The emphasis in the title
text must be lifted recursively — emphasis becomes `<i>` per the decided
stylistic mapping.

### Bare sub-sub-heading with `inline code`

Triple-hash bare heading lifts to `<sub-sub-section>`. Inline code in the
title text must also be lifted recursively.

# Top-level with **strong** text and ~~strikethrough~~

Strong (bold) lifts to `<b>`; strikethrough lifts to `<s>` — both per the
decided mappings.

#### Depth-4 heading passes through as `<h4>`

A depth-4 heading exceeds eHTML's three section levels. It is **not**
mapped to a section and **not** mapped to `<b>`. It passes through as a
literal `<h4>` element with an informative diagnostic emitted.

##### Depth-5 heading passes through as `<h5>`

Same treatment as depth-4.

###### Depth-6 heading passes through as `<h6>`

Same treatment.

# Bare heading inside named-tag content

<aside | An aside containing a recursive heading.

## Nested bare heading inside aside content

The bare `##` heading appearing inside the aside's pipe-content must also
lift — the gate's walker recurses into enscribeTag content arrays.

>
